></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOURI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO, HIROTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKA, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OWAKI, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, TAMOTSU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of crosslinked-rubber reclamation by which various crosslinked rubbers difficult to reclaim can be reclaimed. The method of reclaiming a crosslinked rubber (10) comprises a reclamation step in which a shear force is applied to the crosslinked rubber (10), wherein the maximum pressure in the reclamation step is 1.5 MPa or higher.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de récupération de caoutchouc réticulé permettant de récupérer différents caoutchoucs réticulés difficiles à récupérer. Le procédé de récupération d'un caoutchouc (10) réticulé consiste à appliquer, dans une phase de récupération, une force de cisaillement au caoutchouc (10) réticulé, la pression maximale dans la phase de récupération étant supérieure ou égale à 1,5 MPa.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to thi